INT. DRIVE-IN THEATER PROJECTION BOOTH - NIGHT

A cramped concrete box above the snack bar. Two projectors, dusty. A shelf of film cans. One small window overlooking a lot of weeds and a blank screen leaning in the dark.

Six people crowd the booth. Rain drums the roof. A lantern sits on an overturned can, throwing their shadows huge.

DOCTOR MARGUERITE OYELARAN-STACK (50s, medical bag, cardigan) kneels by a figure lying on the floor under a coat.

The coat covers the face of PATRICK "PADDY" GALLAGHER-NWOSU (30s, projectionist), who is not moving.

SHERIFF HOLCOMB JABLONSKI (60s, rain slicker, flashlight) stands at the door, back to the wall, watching the stairs.

TWO TEENAGERS huddle by the window. They are JUNIPER PARK-MBEKI (16, letterman jacket) and her brother SAUL (17, headphones around his neck, shaking).

By the film shelf, an old woman, MRS. ODETTE ABERNATHY-VOSS (70s, shawl, a thermos clutched like a talisman).

MARGUERITE
He's gone.

SAUL
He can't be.

JUNIPER
Saul, don't.

MRS. ABERNATHY
He was fine at the second reel.

HOLCOMB
Everybody quiet.

They fall quiet. Rain. And below the rain, a slow scrape on the stairs. Something dragging.

SAUL
That's him.

MARGUERITE
He's right there, Saul.

SAUL
Then who's on the stairs?

JUNIPER
Oh God.

MRS. ABERNATHY
Don't say His name. Not in here.

HOLCOMB
Lock the door.

JUNIPER
There's no lock!

SAUL
Use the can! Use a film can!

MARGUERITE
Hold on, hold on, everyone--

HOLCOMB
(over her)
Get back from the door!

SAUL
(over him)
It's coming up!

JUNIPER
(over both)
Saul, shut UP!

MRS. ABERNATHY
(over everyone)
It wants the projector!

They all stop. Look at her.

MRS. ABERNATHY (CONT'D)
(quietly)
It always wants the projector.

The scrape reaches the top of the stairs. Stops. The lantern flame leans toward the door, as if drawn.

HOLCOMB
(muttering)
Nothing there. Nothing there.

Something knocks. Three times. Soft. Almost polite.

SAUL
Don't open it.

MARGUERITE
Nobody's opening it.

The door handle turns.

JUNIPER
(whispering)
It's locked, right? Tell me it's locked.

HOLCOMB
There's no lock, I said!

The door swings in. Empty landing. Wet footprints on the concrete, leading in.

The footprints lead to Paddy's body.

The coat slides slowly off his face.

MARGUERITE
(to herself)
No pulse. I checked. I checked.

Paddy's eyes open. White. Wet. He looks at the projectors.

PADDY
(a rasp)
Roll it.

Every projector in the booth clatters to life by itself. Light erupts against the blank screen outside, and a figure of the sheriff, thirty feet tall, begins to move across it.

Holcomb looks over his shoulder at the window. At himself on the screen. He raises his flashlight.

HOLCOMB
(barely)
That's not me.

On the screen, the giant Holcomb turns and looks into the booth.
